{"id":"mahabharata-12-108","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":108,"title":"अष्टाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 108 · Confederacies and their weakness","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks about the dharma of the four orders and the way of life of each, and Bhishma tells of the weakness of confederacies, which are destroyed by greed and anger. He says that leaders of such clans must keep unity and consult the wise.","kn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ವರ್ಣಗಳ ಧರ್ಮ ಮತ್ತು ಜೀವನ ವಿಧಾನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಲೋಭ, ಕ್ರೋಧದಿಂದ ನಾಶವಾಗುವ ಗಣರಾಜ್ಯಗಳ ದೌರ್ಬಲ್ಯವನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಂತಹ ಕುಲಗಳ ನಾಯಕರು ಒಗ್ಗಟ್ಟು ಉಳಿಸಿ ಜ್ಞಾನಿಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂಪರ್ಕಿಸಬೇಕು.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर चारों वर्णों के धर्म और जीविका के बारे में पूछते हैं, और भीष्म गणराज्यों की दुर्बलता बताते हैं जो लोभ और क्रोध से नष्ट होते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि ऐसे कुलों के नेताओं को एकता रखनी और ज्ञानियों से परामर्श करना चाहिए।","te":"నాలుగు వర్ణాల ధర్మం, జీవన విధానం గురించి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; లోభం, కోపంతో నాశనమయ్యే గణరాజ్యాల బలహీనతను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. అలాంటి వంశాల నాయకులు ఐక్యత నిలిపి జ్ఞానులను సంప్రదించాలంటాడు.","ta":"நான்கு வருணங்களின் தர்மம், வாழும் முறை பற்றி யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, பேராசையாலும் சினத்தாலும் அழியும் குடியரசுகளின் பலவீனத்தைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். அத்தகைய குலங்களின் தலைவர் ஒற்றுமையைக் காத்து ஞானிகளைக் கலந்தாலோசிக்க வேண்டும் என்கிறார்.","ml":"നാലു വർണ്ണങ്ങളുടെ ധർമ്മങ്ങളെയും ഓരോന്നിന്റെയും ജീവിതരീതിയെയും കുറിച്ച് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോഗമുള്ള സഖ്യങ്ങൾ ദുരാഗ്രഹത്താലും കോപത്താലും നശിക്കുന്നു എന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. അത്തരം ഗോത്രങ്ങളുടെ നേതാക്കൾ ഐക്യം നിലനിർത്തുകയും ജ്ഞാനികളോട് ആലോചിക്കുകയും വേണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.108; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशां शूद्राणां च परंतप ।\nधर्मो वृत्तं च वृत्तिश्च वृत्त्युपायफलानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scourge of foes, you have told me the dharma, conduct and livelihood of Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas and Shudras, and the means and results of livelihoods..."}},{"n":2,"text":"राज्ञां वृत्तं च कोशश्च कोशसंजननं महत् ।\nअमात्यगुणवृद्धिश्च प्रकृतीनां च वर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...the conduct of kings, the treasury and its great means of increase, the growth of ministers' virtues, and the prospering of the subjects..."}},{"n":3,"text":"षाड्गुण्यगुणकल्पश्च सेनानीतिस्तथैव च ।\nदुष्टस्य च परिज्ञानमदुष्टस्य च लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...the sixfold policy and its qualities, the policy of the army, how to recognise the wicked and the signs of the good..."}},{"n":4,"text":"समहीनाधिकानां च यथावल्लक्षणोच्चयः ।\nमध्यमस्य च तुष्ट्यर्थं यथा स्थेयं विवर्धता ॥","meaning":{"en":"...the signs of equals, inferiors and superiors set out properly, and how one should stand to satisfy a middling king while growing..."}},{"n":5,"text":"क्षीणसंग्रहवृत्तिश्च यथावत्संप्रकीर्तिता ।\nलघुनादेशरूपेण ग्रन्थयोगेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"...and the conduct of the impoverished who must gather resources, all properly described, Bharata, briefly, as in a compact treatise."}},{"n":6,"text":"विजिगीषोस्तथावृत्तमुक्तं चैव तथैव ते ।\nगणानां वृत्तिमिच्छामि श्रोतुं मतिमतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have also told me the conduct of one who seeks to conquer. Now I wish to hear the way of the gana confederacies, best of the wise."}},{"n":7,"text":"यथा गणाः प्रवर्धन्ते न भिद्यन्ते च भारत ।\nअरीन्हि विजिगीषन्ते सुहृदः प्राप्नुवन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"How do confederacies grow and not split, Bharata? They seek to conquer their enemies and gain friends."}},{"n":8,"text":"भेदमूलो विनाशो हि गणानामुपलभ्यते ।\nमन्त्रसंवरणं दुःखं बहूनामिति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the ruin of confederacies is seen to have division as its root; and keeping counsel secret is hard among many, I think."}},{"n":9,"text":"एतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं निखिलेन परंतप ।\nयथा च ते न भिद्येरंस्तच्च मे ब्रूहि पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear this in full, scourge of foes, and tell me how they may not be split, O king."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"गणानां च कुलानां च राज्ञां च भरतर्षभ ।\nवैरसंदीपनावेतौ लोभामर्षौ जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"For confederacies, families and kings alike, bull of the Bharatas, greed and impatience are the two things that kindle enmity."}},{"n":11,"text":"लोभमेको हि वृणुते ततोऽमर्षमनन्तरम् ।\nतौ क्षयव्ययसंयुक्तावन्योन्यजनिताश्रयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"One first embraces greed, and impatience follows. Both bring loss and expense, each producing the other's support."}},{"n":12,"text":"चारमन्त्रबलादानैः सामदानविभेदनैः ।\nक्षयव्ययभयोपायैः कर्शयन्तीतरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With spies, counsel, force and gifts, with conciliation, giving and division, with loss, expense and fear, they wear each other down."}},{"n":13,"text":"तत्र दानेन भिद्यन्ते गणाः संघातवृत्तयः ।\nभिन्ना विमनसः सर्वे गच्छन्त्यरिवशं भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, confederacies that live in unity are split by gifts; split and sullen, all of them go under the enemy's power through fear."}},{"n":14,"text":"भेदाद्गणा विनश्यन्ति भिन्नाः सूपजपाः परैः ।\nतस्मात्संघातयोगेषु प्रयतेरन्गणाः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Confederacies perish by division; divided, they are well worked on by foes. So confederacies should always strive for solid union."}},{"n":15,"text":"अर्था ह्येवाधिगम्यन्ते संघातबलपौरुषात् ।\nबाह्याश्च मैत्रीं कुर्वन्ति तेषु संघातवृत्तिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth is gained by the strength and manliness of union, and outsiders make friends with those who live united."}},{"n":16,"text":"ज्ञानवृद्धान्प्रशंसन्तः शुश्रूषन्तः परस्परम् ।\nविनिवृत्ताभिसंधानाः सुखमेधन्ति सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Praising those old in knowledge and serving one another, with intrigue set aside, they prosper happily everywhere."}},{"n":17,"text":"धर्मिष्ठान्व्यवहारांश्च स्थापयन्तश्च शास्त्रतः ।\nयथावत्संप्रवर्तन्तो विवर्धन्ते गणोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Establishing righteous practices according to the texts and acting properly, the best confederacies grow."}},{"n":18,"text":"पुत्रान्भ्रातॄन्निगृह्णन्तो विनये च सदा रताः ।\nविनीतांश्च प्रगृह्णन्तो विवर्धन्ते गणोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Restraining their sons and brothers and ever devoted to discipline, and favouring the disciplined, the best confederacies grow."}},{"n":19,"text":"चारमन्त्रविधानेषु कोशसंनिचयेषु च ।\nनित्ययुक्ता महाबाहो वर्धन्ते सर्वतो गणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always attentive to the arrangement of spies and counsel and the storing of the treasury, confederacies grow on every side, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":20,"text":"प्राज्ञाञ्शूरान्महेष्वासान्कर्मसु स्थिरपौरुषान् ।\nमानयन्तः सदा युक्ता विवर्धन्ते गणा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always honouring the wise, the brave, the great archers and the steadfast in action, confederacies prosper, O king."}},{"n":21,"text":"द्रव्यवन्तश्च शूराश्च शस्त्रज्ञाः शास्त्रपारगाः ।\nकृच्छ्रास्वापत्सु संमूढान्गणानुत्तारयन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealthy men, heroes, those who know weapons and have mastered the texts rescue confederacies bewildered in dire straits."}},{"n":22,"text":"क्रोधो भेदो भयो दण्डः कर्शनं निग्रहो वधः ।\nनयन्त्यरिवशं सद्यो गणान्भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anger, division, fear, punishment, harassment, restraint and killing quickly bring confederacies under the enemy's power, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्मान्मानयितव्यास्ते गणमुख्याः प्रधानतः ।\nलोकयात्रा समायत्ता भूयसी तेषु पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So those chiefs of the confederacy should be honoured above all, for the greater part of the world's affairs depends on them, O king."}},{"n":24,"text":"मन्त्रगुप्तिः प्रधानेषु चारश्चामित्रकर्शन ।\nन गणाः कृत्स्नशो मन्त्रं श्रोतुमर्हन्ति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Secret counsel must be kept among the leaders, and spies too, scourge of enemies; the whole body of the confederacy should not hear the counsel, Bharata."}},{"n":25,"text":"गणमुख्यैस्तु संभूय कार्यं गणहितं मिथः ।\nपृथग्गणस्य भिन्नस्य विमतस्य ततोऽन्यथा ।\nअर्थाः प्रत्यवसीदन्ति तथानर्था भवन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The welfare of the confederacy should be handled together by its chief men; but if the confederacy is split into separate parts and at odds, affairs fail and misfortunes come."}},{"n":26,"text":"तेषामन्योन्यभिन्नानां स्वशक्तिमनुतिष्ठताम् ।\nनिग्रहः पण्डितैः कार्यः क्षिप्रमेव प्रधानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they are divided from one another and each acts on his own strength, the learned should quickly restrain the leaders."}},{"n":27,"text":"कुलेषु कलहा जाताः कुलवृद्धैरुपेक्षिताः ।\nगोत्रस्य राजन्कुर्वन्ति गणसंभेदकारिकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quarrels born in families, if neglected by the family elders, bring about the splitting of the clan, king, and of the confederacy."}},{"n":28,"text":"आभ्यन्तरं भयं रक्ष्यं सुरक्ष्यं बाह्यतो भयम् ।\nअभ्यन्तराद्भयं जातं सद्यो मूलं निकृन्तति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fear from within must be guarded against; fear from outside is easily guarded. Fear born from within cuts down the root at once."}},{"n":29,"text":"अकस्मात्क्रोधलोभाद्वा मोहाद्वापि स्वभावजात् ।\nअन्योन्यं नाभिभाषन्ते तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, from sudden anger, greed or delusion, or from their own nature, they do not speak to each other, that is the sign of their defeat."}},{"n":30,"text":"जात्या च सदृशाः सर्वे कुलेन सदृशास्तथा ।\nन तु शौर्येण बुद्ध्या वा रूपद्रव्येण वा पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All are alike in birth, and alike in family, but not in valour, intelligence, looks or wealth."}},{"n":31,"text":"भेदाच्चैव प्रमादाच्च नाम्यन्ते रिपुभिर्गणाः ।\nतस्मात्संघातमेवाहुर्गणानां शरणं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through division and carelessness confederacies are subdued by their enemies; therefore they say that union is the great refuge of confederacies."}}]}]}